  "notes": [
    "Manually read every eligible production file: index.ts (265 lines), src/controller.ts (276 lines), and src/review.ts (68 lines), plus package.json and openclaw.plugin.json. All eight files under the plugin root are partitioned and their working-tree bytes match the pinned commit.",
    "All production relative imports stay inside extensions/advisor. The only external production imports are the public openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry module and node:crypto; there is no additional plugin-owned/shared shipped source outside this root and no installed-dependency or SDK-implementation crawl.",
    "SDK public package exports and plugin-entry.ts establish the public specifier and imported exports. Its register option resolves through OpenClawPluginDefinition.register to OpenClawPluginApi; api.runtime is typed PluginRuntime. Those contract reads establish provenance only, not extra plugin-scope source records.",
    "The sole production createAdvisorController caller passes api.logger unchanged. Calls through deps.logger.info and deps.logger.warn therefore retain the API logger provenance; other controller-owned dependency functions and returned controller methods do not become public API/runtime paths.",
    "resolveSchedule has one production call with api.pluginConfig. Its config[key] read is statically resolved by the two literal read calls to everyToolCalls and everyMinutes. The standalone api.pluginConfig passing occurrence independently establishes that shorter member path.",
    "PluginServiceSchedulerV1 is explicitly imported as a type and used as a scheduler annotation. The service callback ctx.scheduler, its AbortSignal, scheduler methods, event callback ctx methods and hook context values are their own public/context contracts, not aliases of OpenClawPluginApi or PluginRuntime; no lookalike API/runtime paths are invented.",
    "The runtime.config.current return value and forkSession result are not runtime handles. Result/config fields, plugin-owned object members, built-in AbortSignal operations and controller wrappers are not expanded into runtime-member findings.",
    "The manifest declares descriptive metadata, activation, configuration schema/groups and UI hints, but no channels, providers, skills, commandAliases, cliCommands or contracts entries; it contributes no manifest-contract identities.",
    "Source-phase classifications preserve the ordinary runtime import and explicit inline type import at the same SDK module site. The module is mixed; definePluginEntry is runtime; PluginServiceSchedulerV1 is type. Test-only SDK imports do not enter the answer key."
